**Proposed fix.** Update the instruction emitter in\n`src/arcpuzzles/review_full_draw.py` and the copied RETURN-GUIDE template to show\neither `--enumerate-schedule-period --schedule-seed 0` on after checks, or both\nthe census and receipt-attachment commands when a schedule exists. The guide\nexplains enumeration but its default command omits attachment. Preserve source,\nseed and rotation-policy binding and reject stale receipts. No shared source\nchange is included in this task delta."},{"id":"F2","text":"Repair packet-wide tests in a separate maintenance scope\n\n**Evidence.** The full repository run has 1,002 passed, 17 failed, 3 skipped and\n18 passed subtests. `checks/repository-suite/TRIAGE.md`, `triage.json`, full log\nand JUnit classify each failure: 13 environment related (12 process/PID\nobservation, one socket permission), two shared-tool assertion mismatches and\ntwo unrelated archival fixtures whose causes remain unresolved. Twenty-five\nrelevant files match the original ZIP, but baseline execution was not repeated.\n\n**Proposed fix.** Make process-test prerequisites explicit where PID observations\nare inconsistent, separate socket restrictions from product failures, update\nthe two stale assertions only after confirming intended behavior, and investigate\nthe archival identities/domain expectation independently. Rerun those affected\nscopes. Do not infer whole-repository green from the assigned task's 61 passes.\nThe permitted task-local repair and regressions are already included; unrelated\nshared-suite edits require a different change scope."}],"packet_id":"6d4bcfef35cbdd009443c1d190c586508065c404d2cab90ac7cbf9431f3eb0c1","reviewer_blind_solve":{"attempt_count":1,"attempt_intents":{"solve-blind/attempts/0001/report.json":"solve"},"attempt_reports":["solve-blind/attempts/0001/report.json"],"earlier_rule_exposure":"no","feedback_policy":"visible_only","generator_hash":"a30c04fd21088af1a4f89745861eb389b2745ded0ccbe199c9b40774294b10fb","instance_has